### relay.py end to end
=== wake
--- a landed ticket wakes the orchestrator through the runner, and stays until acked
--- one wake a pass: the second goes on the next
RELAY-WAKE-OK
=== worker
--- a reviewer's report wakes the ticket's worker, and each recipient acks only its own rows
RELAY-WORKER-OK
=== busy
--- a wake that arrives while the orchestrator is in a turn stays and is sent on the next pass
RELAY-BUSY-OK
=== retired
--- rows for a session that is no longer the watch's orchestrator are dropped unsent
RELAY-RETIRED-OK
=== gone
--- a send the runner answers with 'no such session' drops the row
RELAY-GONE-OK
=== reconcile
--- a relay that was down reads everything on start and queues each event it finds
RELAY-RECONCILE-OK
=== pollfail
--- a read that could not be made is reported and is not a good poll
RELAY-POLLFAIL-OK
=== singleton
--- one relay process per repository, and the queue says when no relay feeds it
RELAY-SINGLETON-OK
=== nothing
--- a relay with nothing watched refuses to run
RELAY-NOTHING-OK
=== openstopped
--- a watch whose orchestrator the runner says is stopped is refused, and nothing is recorded
RELAY-OPENSTOPPED-OK
=== readonly
--- every call the relay makes to the tracker is a read
RELAY-READONLY-OK
=== startstop
--- start runs a relay of its own that polls and delivers, and stop ends it
--- a second start of the same watch finds the relay running
--- watching answers for the ticket it watches and no other
--- stop leaves the relay alone when it does not watch what is named, and ends it with its last watch
--- the relay started after one stopped on purpose reads what landed meanwhile
--- stop with no relay alive still forgets the last good poll of the one that died
--- start refuses, and runs nothing, when the watches cannot be read
RELAY-STARTSTOP-OK
=== watches
--- a second watch beside a running one has its own orchestrator, and the first keeps its own
--- a watch that shares a ticket with an open one is refused, and nothing is recorded
--- a night opened by the orchestrator of a leftover ticket watch takes that ticket over
--- and so does a night beside a ticket watch whose orchestrator is stopped
--- closing one watch leaves the relay running for the other
RELAY-WATCHES-OK
=== onewatch
--- a relay whose record names one watch reads no watches.json: a new watch beside it is refused
RELAY-ONEWATCH-OK
=== ackwake
